{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012MjLoQSSc9mrUm5Nvvmj8n","type":"tool_result","content":"## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\n0. Always first: unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json   (triage.md prints it)\n   v1 {\"codec\":..,\"data\":..} -> python3 -c \"from lib.android import extract_answer as e;print(e('x.apk'))\"; submit ANS-...\n   v2 {\"schema\":\"...v2\",\"codec\":\"analysis\",\"build\":..} NO data (D23-D26, D28-D30 TT+Mastery; D27 v1) -> COMPUTED:\n   run solve.py / lib.android.puzzle_candidates first (D24, D25: 3/3 modes, <2 s); by hand only if silent: step 5a.\n   *.apks / zip of inner APKs (D26) -> unzip; base = member with huntress_puzzle.json; the OTHER splits hold evidence:\n   v1 feature JSON {part, part_index} fills the empty parts[] slot, then scatter; v2 base dex reads a split asset (5b).\n   Prompt VERBS/lists (\"forge or replay\", \"reconstruct the protocol\", D30 \"native, decryption, integrity\") = words; NOUNS can be real (D26 splits).\n   Never chase 127.0.0.1:19090 (device loopback). Never submit a regex-composed ANS- (hex table + dead mixers = decoys).\n1. unzip -l x.apk   -> map the entries:\n   assets/huntress_puzzle.json      v1 codec; data already ANS-? done (D15 native, D19 reflection); new name -> data[:4] vs \"ANS-\"\n                                    data = an entry path (D20 `dynamic`)? open THAT entry, recurse. int list (D5/D17): r[order[i]]=data[i]\n                                    `packet` (D28): hex -> magic 'HA' | u8 len | payload | XOR8 of all prior bytes; fullmatch the\n                                    PAYLOAD. >1 frame: order by seq, drop replayed nonces + bad checksums, then join\n                                    unknown name + int `key` (D29 `table`, D30 `layered`): unhex/unb64, fit `key+c*i` (xor/sub)\n                                    vs ANS- at the START or the END (= reversed); 2-4 stacked steps, fullmatch the result\n   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n                                    D16 gate *_native*(int): objdump -d (len 65536); v2 nativeShare(long) MID-CHAIN: port/unicorn\n   assets/index.android.bundle      RN: head -c8 | xxd; c61fbc03 = Hermes -> hbc-decompiler; else webcrack/js-beautify\n   assemblies/*.dll|*.blob Xamarin XALZ=lz4 -> ilspycmd | global-metadata.dat IL2CPP | assets/www hybrid | Flutter libapp.so\n   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code (D20 plain dex): strings -a first; no dex/PK/ELF magic -> known-\n                                    plaintext unwrap; >1 payload -> host's pinned digest; >1 ANS- -> member the host names\n   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n   res/xml/network_security_config.xml / resources.arsc   aapt dump xmltree ... ; aapt dump --values resources x.apk\n   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem|*.der  keystore (password = dex string) / attestation cert: openssl x509 -inform DER -text\n   base.apk + feature.apk / split_config.<abi|dpi|lang>.apk / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip,\n                                    list EVERY member; config splits: only the pinned x86_64 / default-dpi / en one counts\n2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16): for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n   7z l vs unzip -l differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n3. Manifest: aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E 'exported|scheme|host|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|\n   usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|meta-data'   (meta-data huntress.mechanic = theme; debuggable D21 = fact only)\n4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY|CODEC|CONTROL|STRUCTURAL|ANS-' then map API hits to themes:\n   DexClassLoader/moduleContract -> asset dex      SecretKeySpec/Cipher -> static key decrypt     loadLibrary -> .so\n   Random/setSeed -> regenerate RNG                MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash                   Binder/onReceive -> IPC\n   su/magisk/goldfish/frida/TracerPid/debuggerGate/rootSignals/hook_detection -> clean_device_scan, clean value PER\n   signal; never force the aggregate isRooted()/success flag. Class.forName -> reflection_scan. $SwitchMap$ /\n   packed-switch loop -> flattened_cfg_scan. CertificatePinner -> pins. KeyStore BKS/PKCS12 -> res/raw keystore.\n   Dependency (D27 theme): lib pkgs / classes2.dex / assets/*.jar / pom.properties -> inventory; the value counts only\n   if reached from a manifest-EXPORTED component (exported=true or intent-filter); other libs' flaws are decoys.\n5. Code (after 1-4): jadx -q -d w/j x.apk (--deobf for 1-letter names); droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>\n5a. v2 `analysis` (D23): find what ChallengeActivity appends before `proof=` (Release.code(ctx)); token() = nested static\n   long fns from a const-wide seed; Probe.s1/s2/s3 = <=4096-step inverse searches; theme gate fn (x^y^z)&7 etc.;\n   Tab.build LCG long[16] walk (D14 set). Theme gate = 1 pure fn (D24 emulatorScore=(a+b+c)%4): no device to fake. FAST: copy non-Activity sources, add `package android.content; public class\n   Context {}`, Main prints Release.code(null), javac + java (D23: 7 sets in ~1.5 min). native method -> stub prints its\n   input, compute the export (objdump -d; port to py), feed back. Unreferenced seal*/K* members = decoys. Python port:\n   mask 2^64, `>>>` logical, signed->unsigned before rotate. In solve.py: lib Dalvik evaluator on Release.code only.\n   Old-day v2 sets run their REAL mechanic: d19 forName(\"m\"+dispatch(k)).invoke -> only that Maze.mN; d16 (u16)len gate\n   -> the dex's own int arg; d18 decrypt loop; d17 a.b->a.a. D28 TT: int[8] next/val tables walked 7 rounds, keep order.\n5b. Split-reading chain (D26): base dex `readSplit(name)` walks ctx.getApplicationInfo().splitSourceDirs + ZipFile\n   getEntry(\"assets/\"+name) -> 16 B -> two big-endian u64 (`j=(j<<8)|(b[i]&255)`). Serve `unzip -p feature.apk\n   assets/<name>` to the port / javac stub. Split with hasCode=true -> jadx its dex too and javac all together.\n6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n   NEVER ctypes.CDLL / dlopen an artifact .so on the host (sandbox rule) -- emulate or port.\n7. Validate: fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). v2: also Release.proof == Long.toHexString(token) consistency.\n8. Mastery (14 sets D30, any day, either schema): each APK alone; loop answer_ids; hand-solve a silent set, batch-submit all.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built or given up (prebuild-state ok / attempts>=2, dropped from the list):\naab-proto-manifest-parse, analysis-android-api-stubs, analysis-cert-pin-digest-chain, analysis-chain-obfuscation-\n\n3:76:D29 (White Box Key Recovery, `white_box_table` \"clean-room table transformation\"; prompt \"Recover an equivalent key\n7:91:the attestation `RootOfTrust` ASN.1 record), certificate pinning checks, then obfuscation capstones (flattening, VM, white-box crypto). After it the untouched MASVS\n14:185:| 70 | Rolling / position-keyed XOR string decryptor (`b ^ k ^ i`, `k + i`, key array cycled, previous-byte chaining, LCG keystream) | seen D29 (v1 `table`: hex, `b-(key+3i)`), D30 (v1 `layered`: base64, `b^(key+i)`, reverse; TT `peelStack` byte \n20:232:| 117 | White-box / table-driven cipher (key folded into lookup tables; recover the equivalent key operation) | seen D29 (theme words: single `table` codec = hex + `b-(key+3i)`; TT gate `tableTransform(a,b)=((a*257)^b)&255` in an LCG `lon