t target; the other same-shape methods are decoys. Regression: libarena.so export decrypting 'm5' and\n  {\"id\": \"puzzle-key-from-variant-identity\", \"concept\": \"codec key/seed derived from the per-variant identity (v2 `build`, package suffix v<12 hex>, case ref MOB-NN-<10 hex>, client_secret) instead of a JSON `key`\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"So far the identity never fed the answer. If a v1 puzzle drops `key` or a v2 seed reads the asset `build`, try keys int(build[:2],16), int(build,16)&0xff, sum/xor of identity bytes, the package suffix bytes, String.hashCode of the case ref; always anchored on the ANS- fullmatch. Read build/package/case ref from the APK (JSON, manifest\n  {\"id\": \"request-signing-canonical-reconstruct\", \"concept\": \"app-to-backend request signature (canonical string + HMAC/nonce/timestamp headers) computed statically (row 115)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If the capstone makes 'proving the same backend effect' real: evaluate Mac.getInstance(HmacSHA256/HmacSHA1).init(SecretKeySpec(key)).doFinal(canonical.getBytes(UTF_8)) and Base64/hex encodings in the evaluator; canonical = method + path + sorted query + nonce + timestamp as built by StringBuilder in the dex; timestamp/nonce from consts. Regression: chain whose token is the\n  {\"id\": \"rpc-stream-frame-decode\", \"concept\": \"streaming/RPC wire formats in an asset or `data` (gRPC 5-byte prefix + protobuf, WebSocket frame + mask, MQTT varint, SLIP/COBS) (row 116)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pure-python decoders: gRPC [flag u8][len u32 BE][protobuf] (reuse protobuf-asset-wire-decode), WebSocket opcode/mask/payload-len 7/16/64 + 4-byte mask xor, MQTT remaining-length varint, SLIP 0xC0/0xDB escapes, COBS. Hook into the v1 race after hex/base64 unwrap.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"race-probe-silent-codec-cue\", \"concept\": \"route a silent race probe on an unknown v1 codec straight to the both-ends ANS- fit\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D30: probe silent on `layered`, LLM worker needed ~40 s (decoded base64, then found key+i xor with `-SNA` at the tail). The cue is now in Recognition cues step 1; keep it in the single-solve prompt and in triage.md's 'what the description suggests' when the codec name is unseen.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"schema-deescalation-guard\", \"concept\": \"timed schema can go BACK (D27: v2 vanished from TT and all 11 Mastery sets)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D27 was solved 3/3 only because v1 decoders still race first in solve.py. Keep that order: v1 puzzle `data` decode -> split-bundle fill -> v2 evaluator -> code scans; never skip v1 because the day number is >= 23 or because yesterday was v2; regression cases from every schema stay in solver/cases.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D26: the cue for `*.apks` (list every member; the evidence lives in the OTHER split) is now in steps 0/1/5b. Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D26 shipped a bare .apks (no toc.pb); config-split / AAB variants are now plausible. github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"generalize-before-stop\", \"concept\": \"carry the hand-solved method into solve.py when a live worker reaches CORRECT first\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D26 repeat: the mastery generalize worker wrote a split-aware eval that never persisted in solve.py. D23: hand-solved TT/Mastery left solve.py without a v2 path; the overnight prebuild fixed it and D24 went 3/3 on the solver alone. Keep the rule: when a timed mode is CORRECT via a live worker, let one generalize worker finish offline and require `hctf solver-test` on the variant-* cases with expected.json filled from co\n  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"}\n]\n```","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c463c0d5-9786-4a75-ad45-321e76fa50a9","uuid":"3febd999-2cc5-406d-8f78-8f03d86ee964","timestamp":"2026-10-31T04:36:47.092Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built or given up (prebuild-state ok / attempts>=2, dropped from the list):\naab-proto-manifest-parse, analysis-android-api-stubs, analysis-cert-pin-digest-chain, analysis-chain-obfuscation-\nhardening, analysis-interface-signal-list-eval, analysis-keystore-cert-api-stubs, analysis-release-code-eval,\nanalysis-self-integrity-stubs, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path, apk-signing-block-\npayload, apk-signing-v3-rotation-lineage, app-update-ver